From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:16:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(circular): rings post as arcs, not 512 fixed chords

A Circular ring was a closed 512-chord polygon at every radius, and the
helix entry's stand-down ramp walked it: one 6 mm hole was 74,131 moves
of 0.006 mm. Each ring-level is now two half-turn arcs about the
authored centre (G3 climb / G2 conventional, the old travel and start
point); the planning polygon's chord count comes from ARC_FIT_TOL (a
power of two dividing the 512-gon certificate), and the zig-zag ramp on
a ring flies helical arcs on the ring (same legs, length and angle).
The repro is 417 moves; verify verdicts are unchanged.

Fixes #1558

